1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:04,830
In 1974, Stephen King checked into Room 217.

2
00:00:04,910 --> 00:00:06,700
The Stanley Hotel, Colorado.

3
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:07,780
Closing for winter.

4
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:08,730
Nearly empty.

5
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:11,670
That night he dreamed of a fire hose chasing his son.

6
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:14,860
One cigarette later, he had the bones of The Shining.

7
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:17,010
But the staff tell an older story.

8
00:00:17,370 --> 00:00:19,080
June 1911.

9
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:21,510
Gas is leaking in 217.

10
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:24,900
Chambermaid Elizabeth Wilson walks in with a lit candle.

11
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:28,250
The blast drops her through the floor, into the dining room.

12
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:32,230
Guests now report unpacked suitcases, lights switching on and off.

13
00:00:32,390 --> 00:00:34,260
The legend says she's still on shift.

14
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:37,130
But the record says Elizabeth Wilson survived.

15
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:39,180
She went back to work at the hotel.

16
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:42,710
The woman said to haunt 217 didn't die in it.

17
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:44,880
And the hotel sells ghost tours.

18
00:00:45,830 --> 00:00:47,660
So who unpacked this suitcase?

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:48,790
Nobody knows.

20
00:00:48,810 --> 00:00:50,180
But it started like this:
